== instructions for the ESP32 v1 Dev board - pinouts may vary for other devices ==

We're doing a basic README so the repo looks nicer - but this takes a NMEA stream from a UBlox GPS, tweaks the GPS to high speed serial, turns on all the sentences, exposes a Bluetooth Serial device, and then outputs a sanitized 4800 baud stream to the Kenwood TM-D700a and probably others. Hook up your gps to the 3.3 or 5v rail, take its TTL level TX (NMEA out) to pin 16 (UART 2 RX) and put the TTL  level RX (NMEA in) to pin 17 (UART 2 TX), then hook the radio's tip pin to D4/GPIO4 and the shield (furthest back ring) to the GND on the chip (there's more than one, so you don't necessarily have to bring everything back to a single pin), and you're in business.

Pin mappings are defs in the top part of the code but they're chosen for Reasons (TM) so understand the chip and its functions before screwing around with it.

